govenv-project-purpose-snapshot-v2
review-index 5
review-rationale "GV130-GV148 plan a governed human-review system around the existing authority model: bounded attention surfaces, append-only Protocol stewardship, portable adversarial reviewers, identity-separated human decisions, and canonical pull-request guidance all strengthen the promise that agents may move fast without outrunning human authority. The complete resulting roadmap therefore remains coherent with the unchanged canonical purpose."
purpose "Turn every repository into a self-governing developer environment: define what valid means once, let agents move fast without outrunning human authority, and reproduce the same tooling, automation, and runtime anywhere."
